//* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
//* RATE LIMITING — SEE src/common/throttler AND docs/concepts/rate-limiting.md
//*
//* 0 = NOTHING IS IN FRONT OF localhost, SO req.ip IS THE SOCKET ADDRESS. THIS IS
//* ALSO WHY THE PRODUCTION VALUE CANNOT BE TESTED FROM A DEV MACHINE: THERE IS NO
//* PROXY HERE TO PRODUCE AN X-Forwarded-For CHAIN TO COUNT.
//* ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
THROTTLE_TRUST_PROXY_HOPS=0

//* SET false TO TURN RATE LIMITING OFF WHILE WORKING ON SOMETHING THAT LEGITIMATELY
//* HAMMERS AN ENDPOINT (SEEDING, A LOAD SCRIPT, AN OTP FLOW YOU ARE RE-RUNNING).
//* PREFER THIS OVER EDITING THE LIMITS — IT KEEPS THE COMMITTED NUMBERS HONEST.
THROTTLE_ENABLED=true

//* GLOBAL TIERS — AT THE SCHEMA DEFAULTS IN src/common/throttler/config/throttler.env.ts.
# THROTTLE_SHORT_TTL_MS=10000
# THROTTLE_SHORT_LIMIT=30
# THROTTLE_LONG_TTL_MS=60000
# THROTTLE_LONG_LIMIT=200
